\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [812, 1670, 1279, 1701], \"page_id\": 5}], \"content\": \"OFFICE OF THE SECRETARY\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [192, 139, 1145, 180], \"page_id\": 6}], \"content\": \"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [192, 202, 1344, 261], \"page_id\": 6}], \"content\": \"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [621, 230, 907, 263], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"Table of Contents\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1177, 319, 1241, 346], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"Page\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1177, 350, 1229, 373], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"A-1\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [262, 346, 1228, 1431], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Treasury financing operations</td><td>A-1</td></tr><tr><td>Summary of fiscal operations</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Budget receipts and expenditures</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Trust accounts, etc.</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>Treasury cash income and outgo</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>General Fund of the Treasury</td><td>13</td></tr><tr><td>Debt outstanding</td><td>14</td></tr><tr><td>Statutory debt limitation</td><td>17</td></tr><tr><td>Debt operations</td><td>18</td></tr><tr><td>United States savings bonds</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><td>Treasury savings notes</td><td>27</td></tr><tr><td>Ownership of Federal securities</td><td>28</td></tr><tr><td>Treasury survey of ownership</td><td>30</td></tr><tr><td>Market quotations</td><td>34</td></tr><tr><td>Yields of Treasury and corporate bonds</td><td>37</td></tr><tr><td>Internal revenue collections</td><td>39</td></tr><tr><td>Monetary statistics</td><td>43</td></tr><tr><td>Capital movements</td><td>47</td></tr><tr><td>Corporations and Certain Other Business-Type Activities - income and expense, and sources and application of funds</td><td>58</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [261, 1478, 315, 1509], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"Note\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [357, 1484, 1078, 1578], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"In those tables where figures have been rounded to a specified unit, all calculations (including percentages) have been made from unrounded figures. Consequently the details may not add to the totals shown.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [84, 7, 234, 31], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"March 1948\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1388, 13, 1423, 33], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"A-1\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [489, 310, 1014, 342], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Treasury Financing Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [93, 426, 552, 455], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"February Certificate Maturity\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [86, 462, 705, 929], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"A one-year issue of 7/8 percent certificates of indebtedness, outstanding in the amount of $3,947 million, matured on February 1, 1948. On January 20, 1948, the Secretary of the Treasury announced the offering of a new one-year 1-1/8 percent certificate in exchange, par for par, for the maturing certificates. Cash subscriptions were not received. The new certificates are dated February 1, 1948, and bear interest from that date at the rate of 1-1/8 percent per annum. Interest will be paid in full with the principal on the maturity date, February 1, 1949. The certificates of indebtedness were issued in bearer form only, in denominations of $1,000, $5,000, $10,000, $100,000, and $1,000,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [84, 973, 701, 1246], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Reports to the Treasury on the ownership of Government securities indicate that on December 31, 1947, about 70 percent of the $3,947 million of certificates maturing February 1 were owned by reporting commercial banks and Federal Reserve Banks. The ownership figures for December 31 are the latest which are available for holdings of both commercial banks and Federal Reserve Banks.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [81, 1270, 701, 1339], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Note: Historical details of Treasury market financing operations are shown in the tables on \\\"Offerings\\\" and \\\"Disposition\\\", respectively, of marketable issues of\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [792, 438, 1414, 708], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Subscription books were opened on January 20 and closed at the close of business January 22. Holdings of the maturing certificates of indebtedness by the Federal Reserve Banks, which amounted to $1,614 million on January 30, were redeemed in full for cash. Exchange subscriptions for the new issue amounted to $2,189 million, leaving $143 million to be paid in cash to holders other than Federal Reserve Banks.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [792, 743, 1346, 775], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bills Refunded and Retired\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [792, 783, 1414, 1252], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Reductions in Treasury bills outstanding again took place in January. The five issues maturing during the month totaled $5.9 billion and the total refunded was $5.6 billion. The first two maturities were $1.3 billion each and the last three $1.1 billion each. The first two maturing issues were refunded in full, but each of the last three was reduced by $100 million. Bill retirements from April 17, 1947, when the first bill reduction occurred, through January 29, 1948, have totaled $2.2 billion. The average rates of discount for the five January offerings, beginning with that dated January 2, were 0.953 percent, 0.950 percent, 0.976 percent, 0.981 percent, and 0.990 percent, respectively.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [861, 1279, 1414, 1342], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"bonds, notes, and certificates of indebtedness, and the tables on \\\"Offerings and Maturities of Treasury Bills\\\", in this issue of the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\".\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [97, 52, 250, 83], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"March 1948\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1423, 56, 1438, 81], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"1\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [495, 110, 1045, 134], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"SUMMARY OF FEDERAL FISCAL OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [656, 157, 870, 179], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [70, 182, 1465, 1589], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Period</th><th colspan=\\\"3\\\">Budget receipts and expenditures</th><th>Trust accounts, etc. - net receipts, or expenditures (-)</th><th>Clearing account</th><th>Net increase in public debt, or decrease (-)</th><th>Net increase in General Fund balance, or decrease (-)</th><th colspan=\\\"4\\\">Level, end of period</th></tr><tr><th></th><th>Net receipts 